  "label": "Stereotype: Black people are natural swimmers or 'water people'",
  "description": "This stereotype, often used in a racially charged context, implies that Black people have an innate or superior ability to swim or interact with water. The meme's text 'kids enjoying some underwater diving' misrepresents the girls' activity and implicitly reinforces this stereotype, potentially exoticizing or mocking their engagement with water. This stereotype is part of a broader pattern of racialized assumptions about physical competence.",
